INT. 24-HOUR LAUNDROMAT - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent hum. Dryers turn like slow planets. Five people, five machines, one wall of washers.

AMARA OSEI (20s) folds a sheet. JOSEPHINE LAMB (60s) reads a paperback. TARIQ HASSAN (30s) stares into dryer four. BENEDETTA ROSSI (50s) feeds quarters into a slot. LUCA FERRIER (20s) is asleep on a plastic chair.

                    AMARA
          You're reading that upside down.

                    JOSEPHINE
          I'm reading it the way the author intended.

                    TARIQ
          Excuse me, do any of you know if wool shrinks at low?

                    BENEDETTA
          It shrinks at everything.

                    TARIQ
          Even love?

                    AMARA
          That was smooth.

                    TARIQ
          That was an accident.

                    JOSEPHINE
          They're the best kind.

                    LUCA
          (waking)
          Is it morning?

                    BENEDETTA
          No, caro. It's 3 a.m. and you owe me a quarter.

                    LUCA
          I do?

                    BENEDETTA
          From last Tuesday.

                    AMARA
          You two know each other?

                    BENEDETTA
          Everyone knows everyone here. It's a laundromat.

                    TARIQ
          Then why have I never seen you before?

                    AMARA
          Maybe you weren't looking.

A dryer buzzes. Nobody moves.
